			"Message": "chore(Element): Restore debuggability and fix IPC payload shape\n\nSynchronize 11 Element submodules to reverse aggressive minification strategies and resolve a critical bug in the native backend. Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker restore full source map generation, revert single-character variable obfuscation, and reformat ESBuild configurations to strict PascalCase naming, ensuring production builds remain debuggable and maintainable.\n\nMountain corrects the `registerView` payload shape by including the required `viewId` key, restoring functionality for extension sidebars that were previously dropping host content due to schema mismatches. Maintain adds recursive JSON array deduplication to ensure build idempotency.\n\nThese changes prioritize developer tooling stability, correct silent failures in the IPC layer, and align the build artifacts with project readability standards while maintaining optimization for production releases.",
			"SHA": "16e66325c50780d70bd532478446b38d3b15154e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T13:38:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 6 submodules for build normalization and release optimization\n\nUpdate six Element submodules to resolve build pipeline inconsistencies, enforce strict PascalCase naming conventions, and optimize production artifacts.\n\nCocoon and Wind refactor ESBuild configurations into modular structures before applying aggressive minification (removing source maps and renaming to single-char identifiers) for release size reduction, while restoring readable, debuggable builds for development. Output follows suit, reformatting its plugin pipeline for readability before minifying entry points and deleting source maps. Rest standardizes its CLI wrapper with consistent quote usage and import ordering. Worker corrects a deviation by reverting inadvertently minified build scripts to readable PascalCase format. Mountain adds native macOS dmg target support, EULA templates, and updated icon assets for the release cycle.\n\nThese changes ensure the editor's build system adheres to project readability standards in development while delivering optimized, deterministic artifacts for production, alongside expanded native distribution capabilities.",
			"SHA": "a43be3f4250cd24c901ed4afac91b4bf3e58f1bd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T09:34:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Synchronize Dependency and Element submodules for v2.2 security and build stability\n\nUpdate the `Dependency` and `Element` submodules to align the editor with the v2.2 correctness pass and build pipeline refinements.\n\nIn `Dependency/Tauri`, correct the inline documentation for `resolve_extension_path` to accurately reflect Unix home directory preservation and Windows drive letter handling, ensuring the `localhost` plugin documentation matches the implementation.\n\nIn `Element`, synchronize multiple submodules to introduce a critical security and observability layer. The `Mountain` backend now enforces strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) via `SecurityContext` and `Validator`, implements AES-256-GCM cryptographically secure IPC with replay protection, and adds native handlers for SCM, Terminal, Text Model, and Extension registry. New `PerformanceDashboard` modules enable distributed tracing with W3C `traceparent` injection. Concurrently, `Cocoon` and `Output` refine ESBuild pipelines for PascalCase compliance and artifact optimization, `Wind` resolves macOS APFS path normalization issues for breadcrumbs, and `Rest` regenerates binaries for telemetry consistency.\n\nThese changes establish a secure, observable native backend, fix critical macOS path resolution bugs, and ensure the extension host builds with optimized yet debuggable artifacts.",
			"SHA": "faa7888802851f5040ad654fcd78f3c117ba5722"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T09:34:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				2
			],
			"Message": "build(Maintain): Remove hardcoded paths from build and codegen scripts\n\nReplace hardcoded `/Volumes/CORSAIR/Developer/macOS/Application/CodeEditorLand/Land` paths in `Maintain/Build/Brotli/PreBake.ts` and `Maintain/Codegen/Sync.ts` with dynamic resolution using `fileURLToPath` and `resolve`.\n\nThis refactors the scripts to calculate `RepoRoot` relative to their own location (e.g., `Land/Maintain/...` -> `Land/`), ensuring the build pipeline and code synchronization logic work correctly across different machines, CI runners, and worktree environments without manual path configuration.\n\nEnables portable execution of the pre-bake step and submodule synchronization regardless of the local mount point or directory structure.",
			"SHA": "066c051d0901ba17e31db85c7b14a6975ecf2901"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:41:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				36
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Implement dual-pipe telemetry (PostHog + OTLP) and unify build instrumentation\n\nIntroduce a dual-telemetry architecture allowing the editor to emit both PostHog events and OpenTelemetry spans simultaneously. Add a new `Container/Compose.yaml` with `Up.sh` and `Down.sh` to spin up a local Jaeger instance for trace visualization, enabling end-to-end distributed tracing across Mountain, Cocoon, Sky, and build processes via a shared `trace_id`.\n\nRefactor the build pipeline (`Maintain/Debug/Build.sh`, `Maintain/Release/Build.sh`) to source `PostHogCapture.sh`, injecting `LandCapture` and `LandCapturePhaseBegin/End` helpers. This instruments every build phase with precise duration metrics and error tracking. Extend `.env.Land.PostHog.Sample` with `OTLPEndpoint`, `OTLPEnabled`, `Capture` (master kill switch), `Trace`, and `Record` configuration keys.\n\nStandardize formatting and ignore rules across `.gitignore`, `.prettierignore`, `rustfmt.toml`, and `Maintain/Format.sh` to ensure consistent exclusion of generated artifacts (`Target`, `Generated`, `Documentation/Rust/doc`, `tauri-codegen-assets`). Update `turbo.json` syntax and `Cargo.toml` formatting.\n\nDeploy PostHog insights scripts (`CreateTierInsights.py`, `PatchTelemetryInsights.py`) to automate dashboard population for tier coverage and error rollups. Add `Maintain/Test/TelemetryTreeShake.sh` to CI to verify production binaries strip all telemetry SDKs. Update `CHANGELOG.md` to document the v2.2 bundled-electron correctness pass.\n\nThis establishes a complete observability surface, replacing ad-hoc logging with structured, queryable telemetry while ensuring production builds remain clean of debugging artifacts.",
			"SHA": "4a8a737a8239d5bbf033e37eaf961485be098b04"
		}
